# Test stub for `sleep`, which very much does exist off-device — this one is
# here to make it instant, not to stand in for a missing command.
#
# Two places in the production code pause by shelling out: bring_up() waits a
# second for netifd to settle, and restore_wan_default() probes three times two
# seconds apart. That is six seconds on EVERY disconnect, and the suite drives
# disconnect from several files, so it was the single largest block of dead
# wall clock in the run — six seconds of a twenty-second file, and nothing
# asserts on the delay itself.
#
# What still runs is the logic around it: the probe loop iterates the same
# number of times, and every command it issues is still issued. Only the
# waiting is skipped.
#
# NOT used for the router-advertisement readiness wait, which pauses with
# ucode's own sleep() builtin and is therefore unaffected — that one is
# shortened honestly, through PROTONVPN_RA_SETTLE_MS (see run.sh).
exit 0
